## What changed

The review agent's coding-plan review (`planning/ta-anchor-refactor-review.md`, still DRAFT — I do not
mark reviews FINAL, that's the review agent's/Dean's call) found 2 MAJOR correctness findings (F1/F2),
5 MAJOR coder-executability blockers (E1-E5), and assorted minor findings (F3-F12, C1, E6-E13). Dean
adjudicated F1 (disable the queueing-model path, must be an explicit error not a silent fallback — see
below) and F2 (confirmed still applies, unaffected by F1) directly in conversation; the rest were
approved for fold-in as proposed. All of it is now folded into `planning/ta-anchor-refactor-plan.md`
across two commits on `plans`:

- `68bda1a1` — F2-F12, C1, E1-E13 (everything except the QM mechanism). Highlights: pinned the anchor
  build site (`runAnalyzersAndScore` return-signature change threading the anchor to
  `collectV2ModelRequest:607`, forbidding the `namedResults[0]` shortcut); added a `cloneAnalyzerResult`
  helper (no `Clone` method exists, `copy()` doesn't compile on a struct) explicitly designed to be
  reusable by PR-2's per-iteration refresh; fixed `withSatEntry` to set `req.Anchor` (87 call sites
  across 4 test files would otherwise go red, including the #1513 goldens); corrected the §9 survivor
  list and made the grep case-insensitive; moved the field-classification test to the `saturation`
  package with a distinct-source fixture; dev-guide section renamed to real headings +
  `saturation-scaling-config.md` added as a second target; checklist renumbered to 15 items.
- `192ae06b` — F1 (queueing-model disable). Dean's requirement: the disable must be an explicit error,
  never a silent fallback to sat-v2, and must not impersonate a working config. Design: `engine.go`'s
  analyzer-selection stays honest (still resolves to `QueueingModelAnalyzerName` when the ConfigMap is
  present); the dispatch switch is redirected to a new `refuseQueueingModel` that logs an `Error` and
  holds every model via the existing `emitSafetyNetMetrics` idiom, instead of calling
  `optimizeQueueingModel`. `engine_queueing_model.go` itself stays 100% untouched (still exercised by
  its own test file, so lint-clean) — classified DEFERRED in §12. Checklist now 16 items.

Plan doc TOC refreshed after each commit. `planning/ta-anchor-refactor-review.md` was not edited by me
(out of my write scope — review docs are the review agent's domain); it stays DRAFT until the review
agent/Dean marks it FINAL, which per the review's own handoff should happen now that the fold-in is
